 |------------|---------|-------------|
 | `registration` | A new asset is added to the registry | server, agent, skill |
 | `deletion` | An existing asset is removed from the registry | server, agent, skill |
+| `scan_complete` | The async post-registration security scan finishes (passed, unsafe, or failed) | server, agent, skill |
+
+### scan_complete Event Payload (Issue #1330)
+
+The async YARA scan that runs after registration emits a `scan_complete`
+event when it finishes, on both the completed and the failed path, so an
+external CI/CD orchestrator can advance the asset lifecycle without polling
+`GET /api/{servers,agents,skills}/{path}/security-scan`:
+
+```json
+{
+    "event_type": "scan_complete",
+    "registration_type": "server",
+    "timestamp": "2026-09-30T12:00:00.000000+00:00",
+    "performed_by": null,
+    "scan": {
+        "path": "/my-server",
+        "scan_timestamp": "2026-09-30T12:01:23.000000+00:00",
+        "is_safe": true,
+        "scan_failed": false,
+        "error_message": null,
+        "critical_issues": 0,
+        "high_severity": 0,
+        "medium_severity": 2,
+        "low_severity": 0,
+        "analyzers_used": ["yara"]
+    }
+}
+```
+
+When the scan itself fails (timeout, scanner error), the event is still sent:
+`is_safe` is `false`, `scan_failed` is `true`, and `error_message` carries the
+error text. The payload is a whitelist of scan outcome fields; it never
+includes raw scanner output (`raw_output`) or credential-derived headers.
+`performed_by` is always `null`: scans are system-initiated.
+
+Note: `scan_complete` fires only from the registration pipeline. The manual
+`POST .../rescan` endpoints return the result synchronously to the caller and
+do not emit events.
 
