+## Consumer Contract (Issue #1330)
+
+Consumers of registration and `scan_complete` webhooks MUST implement the
+following contract.
+
+### Delivery and Ordering
+
+| Property | Guarantee |
+|----------|-----------|
+| Delivery model | Fire-and-forget; at-most-once. No retries or redelivery. |
+| Ordering | NOT guaranteed. Events may arrive out of order (async scans finish at unpredictable times). Consumers must not rely on cross-event ordering. |
+| Emission latency | `registration`/`deletion` fire immediately after persist; `scan_complete` fires when the async scan settles (typically seconds, up to the scan timeout). |
+
+### Idempotency
+
+Duplicate delivery is possible under network-level retries (e.g. connection
+pool reuse). Consumers MUST deduplicate on the tuple:
+
+```
+(event_type, registration_type, card.path or scan.path, timestamp)
+```
+
+An event that fails signature verification must be dropped and logged; it
+MUST NOT trigger lifecycle actions. During a signing-secret rotation, events
+may arrive with either the old or the new signature; treat verification
+failures the same way (drop, never act).
+
+### Signature Verification
+
+When `REGISTRATION_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET` is set, every webhook POST carries:
+
+```
+X-Webhook-Signature: sha256=<hex digest>
+```
+
+The signature is HMAC-SHA256 over the EXACT request body bytes as received
+(not a re-serialization). Verification example:
+
+```python
+import hashlib
+import hmac
+
+def verify_webhook(raw_body: bytes, signature_header: str, secret: str) -> bool:
+    """Constant-time verification of an outbound registry webhook."""
+    if not signature_header.startswith("sha256="):
+        return False  # malformed header: reject before comparing
+    expected = hmac.new(secret.encode("utf-8"), raw_body, hashlib.sha256).hexdigest()
+    return hmac.compare_digest(signature_header.removeprefix("sha256="), expected)
+```
+
+Rules:
+
+- Read the RAW body bytes (`await request.body()`), never `request.json()`
+  followed by re-serialization; JSON formatting differences change the bytes.
+- Always compare with `hmac.compare_digest` (constant time); never `==`.
+- Malformed headers (missing `sha256=` prefix, wrong length, non-hex) are
+  rejected without comparison.
+- Rollout posture: verify-if-present while the registry fleet rolls out the
+  secret, then REQUIRE the header once the cut-over completes.
+
+### Action Safety
+
+A `scan_complete` event with `is_safe=true` authorizes the orchestrator to
+promote an asset only after signature verification succeeds. Never promote on
+an unsigned or unverifiable event; poll
+`GET /api/{type}/{path}/security-scan` instead when in doubt.
+
